course: dictionary
lesson: 3677
title: Fizzy: a word with bubbles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fizzy means full of tiny bubbles of gas. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «A shaken fizzy bottle can spray hard when opened, so never point one at anyone's face.» Shaken and spray tell you that the bubbles push hard, so fizzy must mean full of bubbles.
explain: Ask what word would fit. «Fizzy lemonade» is lemonade with bubbles, so fizzy water has bubbles too. Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word: "A shaken bottle full of bubbles can spray hard when opened" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Fizzy also has a science meaning. The bubbles in fizzy drinks are carbon dioxide gas, and when you open the bottle the gas escapes. «Fizzy drinks often have a lot of sugar and acid, which can harm teeth.» This shows that the word can also be used when you talk about health.
fact: Fizzy means full of tiny bubbles of gas.
fact: «Fizzy» is an adjective, so it can change: fizzier and fizziest.
fact: The bubbles in fizzy drinks are carbon dioxide gas.
fact: Phrases you will meet: fizzy drink, fizzy water, fizzy sweets.
fact: A drink that has lost its bubbles has gone flat.
exercise: «A shaken fizzy bottle can spray hard when opened.» What does fizzy mean? | Empty and dry | Cold and sticky | Thick like soup | *Full of tiny bubbles of gas
exercise: Ella says fizzy water is water with no bubbles. Which is the correct meaning? | Muddy water from a puddle | *Water full of tiny bubbles of gas | Water that is very cold | Water with no bubbles at all
exercise: Which of these is the best example of a fizzy drink? | A dry biscuit | Warm tap water | *A bottle of fizzy lemonade | A plain cup of milk
test: «Baking soda and vinegar make a fizzy reaction, a sign of a chemical change.» What does fizzy show in this sentence? | The mixture is sweet to taste | *Bubbles of gas forming, a sign of a chemical change | A sign that the water is cold | The mixture has frozen solid
test: «Fizzy drinks often have a lot of sugar and acid, which can harm teeth.» What does this sentence tell us? | Sugar makes teeth shine | *Fizzy drinks can be bad for your teeth | Fizzy drinks are good for your teeth | Fizzy drinks have no sugar at all
exam: «Adverts show polar bears sipping fizzy drinks, but real polar bears hardly drink at all.» What is the lesson of this sentence? | Penguins and polar bears live together | *Adverts can show things that are not true to real life | Adverts always show real animals accurately | Polar bears love fizzy drinks
